From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: 8723b: avoid converting RX SNR twice

Carried from the upstream rtw-next commit

  1d72d0db9111c31024e9c019949810bc577f9826
  "wifi: rtw88: 8723b: avoid converting RX SNR twice"
  (Hungyu Lin, 2026-10-10)

which is *not* part of the upstream snapshot this module is built from
(05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d, a torvalds/linux master
snapshot of 2026-11-03): master only merged rtw-next up to the
"rtw-next-2026-10-08" tag, so every 8723B fix from 2026-10-09 onwards
is missing from the tree we ship.

Why we carry it:

rtw8723b_query_phy_status_ofdm() divided the reported SNR by two
when filling pkt_stat->rx_snr and shifted it again when updating
dm_info->rx_snr, so every SNR the driver reported (and the averages
derived from it) was half of what the chip measured.

The upstream fix stores the raw report and converts it once, the way
the other chip drivers do.  We care because the on-device self-check
reads these statistics to judge link quality.
diff --git a/rtw8723b.c b/rtw8723b.c
--- a/rtw8723b.c
+++ b/rtw8723b.c
@@ -1280,7 +1280,7 @@
 	pkt_stat->rx_power[RF_PATH_A] = (val_s8 * 2) - 110;
 
 	pkt_stat->rssi = rtw_phy_rf_power_2_rssi(pkt_stat->rx_power, 1);
-	pkt_stat->rx_snr[RF_PATH_A] = (s8)(phy_status->path_rxsnr[RF_PATH_A] / 2);
+	pkt_stat->rx_snr[RF_PATH_A] = phy_status->path_rxsnr[RF_PATH_A];
 
 	/* signal power reported by HW */
 	val_s8 = phy_status->cck_sig_qual_ofdm_pwdb_all >> 1;
